      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "The paper explicitly names Thr870 as the residue before the junction and 'Try871' (Trp871 in the canonical sequence) as the residue after; Python confirms seq[869]='T' and seq[870]='W', placing the junction squarely in extracellular loop 848\u2013900, 23 residues from the upstream TM boundary (826\u2013847) and 31 residues from the downstream TM boundary (901\u2013918). The 'Try' vs 'Trp' discrepancy is a single-letter typo in the paper; T at 870 matches perfectly and no TY motif exists anywhere in this loop. Surface expression of the tagged construct was validated by flow cytometry (L2, same paper). Full-length human SLC4A2 cloned into BacMam vector; HA tag (YPYDVPDYA) inserted between Thr870 and Trp871 (paper writes 'Try871', a typo for Trp/W, confirmed by the canonical sequence which has W at 871). Construct also carries a C-terminal GFP tag. Expressed in HEK293F cells.",
