      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "[Literature audit 2026-11-05 (deliverome-analysis PR 236), verdict confirmed_shifted: insert_after_residue NULL -> 862: the paper pins the junction on human canonical P04920 (paper numbering: ortholog:mouse, construct species: mouse). Paper (PMID 23271450): \"Oocytes were injected with cRNA encoding wild-type (10 ng) or mutant (50 ng) mAE2 bearing the HA epitope (YPYDVPDYA) inserted between Glu-858 and Ala-859 in the third extracellular loop.\". Audit note: Recoverable: mouse AE2 (P13808) E858|A859 (PLHGCSGSNDSE|AGSSSSSNMTWA) aligns to human P04920 E862|V863 (PLHGCSASNSSE|VDGGENMTWAGA), +4, inside human ECL3; the loop is low-complexity (S/G/N-rich) so +/-2 on the human side. Full text read from PMC4083511. The HA construct is used only for confocal immunofluorescence of fixed, SDS-permeabilized oocytes ('expressed at or near the oocyte surface with near-normal abundance'), not a non-permeabilized accessibility assay; transport assays used untagged cRNA. Row's validation_level not_measured is right.] L3 reports a tolerated HA insertion in the third extracellular loop of mouse AE2 at Glu-858/Ala-859, which is the ortholog of human ECL3 (848\u2013900). Python search confirms no EA motif exists in human ECL3, and the mouse numbering cannot be directly mapped without a full alignment; therefore no exact human residue can be pinned and the site is reported at region level. The loop is large (53 residues) and well-separated from both flanking TM helices, consistent with tolerance of an insertion, but the exact junction within the human loop remains unspecified. Mouse AE2 (mAE2) expressed in Xenopus oocytes via cRNA injection; HA epitope (YPYDVPDYA) inserted between Glu-858 and Ala-859 in the third extracellular loop of mouse AE2. Human SLC4A2 position 858 = S and 859 = N (no EA motif), so the mouse numbering does not transfer directly; the corresponding human loop is 848\u2013900. This is indirect evidence for the same extracellular loop in human SLC4A2.",
